<body>
    <h1 style="padding-top: 1pt;padding-left: 4pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: center;">AGREEMENT FOR (M-WEB PRODUCTS)
        BUSINESS</h1>
    <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
    <p style="padding-left: 13pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">This AGREEMENT FOR (M-WEB PRODUCTS) BUSINESS
        (“Agreement”) is entered on (10<span class="s1">th</span> April 2024) between</p>
    <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
    <h3 style="padding-left: 11pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">Yami IT Solutions Private Limited<span
            class="p">,</span></h3>
    <p style="padding-left: 10pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">a Company incorporated under the Company Act, 2013,
        having its registered office at 322, 3<span class="s1">rd</span> Floor, Rise on Plaza, Varachha Road, Surat-
        395006, India (“Company”)</p>
    <p style="padding-top: 12pt;padding-left: 11pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">And</p>
    <h2 style="padding-top: 12pt;padding-left: 11pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">
        <%=companyName%> bearing GST NO- <%=gstNumber%> registered at <%=companyAddress%> , <%=pincode%>
                        <span class="p">(“Publisher”).</span>
    </h2>
    <h3 style="padding-top: 12pt;padding-left: 11pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">Company <span class="p">and
        </span>The Publisher <span class="p">are individually referred to herein as a “</span>Party<span class="p">” and
            collectively as the “</span>Parties.<span class="p">”</span></h3>
    <p style="padding-top: 12pt;padding-left: 11pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;">NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration
        of the foregoing recitals and the covenants and conditions set forth herein, the Parties hereto agree as
        follows:</p>
    <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
    <ol id="l1">
        <li data-list-text="1.">
            <h3 style="padding-left: 46pt;text-indent: -17pt;text-align: left;">Scope of the Agreement:</h3>
            <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
            <ol id="l2">
                <li data-list-text="1.1.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Company hereby grants to the
                        Publisher, worldwide, non-sublicensable, non-transferable, non-exclusive, and revocable rights
                        to commercially promote the Content (legally licensed or developed content comprising m-web
                        product (s) business in Company’s library) amongst its user community, through the Distribution
                        Channels (as defined in Clause 4.1, 4.2);</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 9pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="1.2.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher shall comply
                        with all the reasonable requests of the Company concerning usage of its content/m-Web Products.
                        Such granted uses of Company’s content/m-Web Products by the Publisher shall not be deemed as
                        the Publisher obtaining any of the ownership of Company’s content/m-Web Products &amp; Company
                        will fully retain the rights and ownership towards its content/m-Web Products.</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 9pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="1.3.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher shall direct its
                        end Users (a person or an entity who avails the Content or any value-added services containing
                        the Content through a Distribution Channel) to the Company’s Content hosting site to avail the
                        Content.</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 9pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="1.4.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The content here means the
                        user accessing Company’s m-Web Products has Games, section, or format added by the Company from
                        time to time.</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 9pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="1.5.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The rights to decisions
                        pertaining to changes, updates, additions, and deletions within the Company’s m- Web products
                        including games and ads will solely remain with the Company.</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 9pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="1.6.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: left;">The Publisher shall accept and
                        implement timely updates of the Company’s m-Web Products.</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 9pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="1.7.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher hereby grants to
                        the Company, worldwide, non-sublicensable, non-transferable, non- exclusive, and royalty-free
                        rights to use the Publisher’s name, its brand name and logo for the Company’s marketing
                        communications, case studies, conference activities.</p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li data-list-text="2.">
            <h3 style="padding-top: 1pt;padding-left: 46pt;text-indent: -17pt;text-align: justify;">Terms of the
                Agreement:</h3>
            <p style="padding-top: 4pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
            <ol id="l3">
                <li data-list-text="2.1.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">This agreement will be in
                        force from the Effective Date and will continue to be in effect for an initial term of 1 (One)
                        year and indefinitely thereafter till the working relationship between the parties. This
                        agreement can be terminated by either party by giving 15 (fifteen) days prior written notice to
                        the other Party, without assigning any reason thereof. In case of any breach of any of the terms
                        of this agreement by the Publisher, the Company can terminate this agreement with immediate
                        effect without prejudice to any other rights available to the Company.</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 9pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.2.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Upon expiration and/or early
                        termination of this Agreement, all rights granted (as mentioned in Clause 1.1) to the Publisher
                        under this Agreement shall cease to exist with immediate effect.</p>
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.3.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The revenue will be calculated
                        based on views and traffic generated by the advertising spaces provide by publishers including
                        any applicable taxes. The Company shall make the payment to the Publisher by bank mode.</p>
                    <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.4.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher shall raise
                        invoices upon the Company based on the affiliate report provided by the Company after
                        confirmation of any adjustments, payment will be made after The Publisher’s revenue exceeds 5000
                        INR (One Thousand Indian Rupees only);</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.5.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Affiliate
                        report implies reports to be shared with the Publisher daily highlighting the revenue and
                        traffic details.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.6.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: justify;">Neither party
                        will indulge in any activities which are against any applicable statutory law.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.7.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Each Party
                        represents, warrants, and covenants to the other Party that it has full capacity and authority
                        to enter, execute, deliver, and perform this Agreement;</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.8.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">This
                        Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India without regard
                        to conflicts of laws principles. The Court of Surat (Gujarat-India) shall have exclusive
                        jurisdiction pertaining to any matter arising out of this agreement.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.9.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">All payments
                        shall be made after the deduction of TDS (withholding tax) in accordance with the applicable
                        laws. All payments will be done in INR.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.10.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Fees payable
                        under this Agreement will be inclusive of applicable Goods and Services Tax, Value Added Tax, or
                        Service Tax that the Publisher is legally obligated to charge under the applicable legislation.
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.11.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: justify;">Payments are
                        to be released within 30 days of receiving the valid invoice from the Publisher.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.12.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Both parties
                        shall keep confidential the information exchanged between parties during the term of this
                        agreement and for three years thereafter. Each party shall keep secret and confidential the
                        technical and business information, financial reports, financial data, employee data, software
                        or firmware code, and all the other information (including emails), knowledge, trade practices,
                        pricing, and secrets communicated to such party by the other party under this Terms and
                        Conditions. Any information accepted whether marked as confidential or not shall be used only as
                        agreed and will not be released to any other third party without the express written permission
                        of the disclosing party. Each party is obliged to prevent any unauthorized copying, use, and/or
                        disclosure of any confidential information of or concerning the other party.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.13.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Either party
                        shall indemnify and hold harmless the other party and its officers, directors, employees, and
                        agents from and against any and all damages, claims, losses, liabilities, costs, or expenses
                        (including reasonable attorney fees and costs) whether incurred due to third party claims or
                        otherwise, arising or resulting from or caused by any breach by either party of any
                        representation, warranty, clause or provision contained in this agreement.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.14.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 1pt;padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">In no event
                        shall either party be liable to the other for any indirect, incidental, consequential, special,
                        or exemplary damages, including lost profits, even if such damages are foreseeable and
                        regardless of whether either party has been advised of the possibility of such damages. In no
                        event shall Company be liable to the Publisher for any amount greater than the amount paid by
                        the Company under this agreement for the most recent three-month period prior to any alleged
                        claim by the Publisher.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="2.15.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Both parties
                        can amend this agreement through a mutual written and signed addendum only. The clauses include
                        but are not limited to the indemnification obligations, restrictions, and compliance,
                        confidentiality shall survive any termination with its nature of survival.</p>
                    <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li data-list-text="3.">
            <h3 style="padding-left: 46pt;text-indent: -17pt;text-align: left;">Restrictions and Compliance:</h3>
            <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
            <ol id="l4">
                <li data-list-text="3.1.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher shall not use
                        the information and data which they have acquired to be used for any business or activity of any
                        Person/entity similar to the business of the Company during a period of two years from the date
                        of early termination/expiration of this agreement</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="3.2.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The
                        Distribution Channel used to promote the Content/m-Web product by the publisher shall not have
                        any content which is obscene/pornographic, defamatory, libellous, slanderous, violent, abusive,
                        gambling, and/or unlawful by any means. Further, the publisher must not use or imply any
                        unethical tools, <span style=" color: #202020;">Clickjacking, deceptive notifications, using VPN
                            (Virtual Private Network) for generating false RPMs/traffic</span>, software piracy,
                        hacking, spam, a proxy, or illegal downloads of any kind and shall not promote on any banned
                        destination.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="3.3.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher
                        shall never attempt to host, copy, modify, reformat, resize, edit, alter, flow tampering,
                        duplicate, port, misrepresent, create backups, store, remove Company’s logo, reverse engineer,
                        or re- engineer the Content/m-Web Products or Company provided integration tools.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="3.4.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 1pt;padding-left: 50pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Publisher
                        shall specify/mention the distribution channel/channels (in case the distribution channels are
                        more than one) under clauses 4.1, and 4.2 and shall not run or integrate or promote the
                        company’s product(s) on any other application, website, destination, and/or platform, without
                        Company’s prior written consent.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="3.5.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher
                        shall integrate Company’s m-Web product(s) in its distribution channel/s within 3 days post
                        receiving the Company’s product(s) integration URL.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="3.6.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: justify;">The Publisher
                        shall understand and strictly comply with the Company’s policies.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="3.7.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">Publisher
                        understands and acknowledges that any breach of conditions mentioned under clause 3 can cause
                        irreparable harm, and huge financial losses to the Company, and in case of any breach of any of
                        the conditions mentioned under clause 3, the Company shall in its sole discretion block
                        Publisher and terminate the agreement with immediate effect without notice and can forfeit all
                        the pending payments of the publisher. The publisher must ethically follow all the Company’s
                        policies stringently. The Company’s decision in this regard shall be final and binding on the
                        Publisher and the Publisher shall accept the decision of the Company without any demur or
                        protest. In addition to the above-mentioned, the Company shall have the right to claim
                        additional damages from the Publisher.</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="3.8.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -21pt;text-align: justify;">If the
                        blocked publisher again gets into the agreement with the Company using any other name, details,
                        or distribution channel then the company shall have the sole and exclusive right to block and
                        terminate the publisher account/agreement again and shall forfeit all the pending payments.
                        Further, the Publisher shall be liable to refund all payments paid by the company for the
                        duplicate account obtained under false pretext till the date of further blocking of the
                        publisher’s account.</p>
                    <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li data-list-text="4.">
            <h3 style="padding-left: 46pt;text-indent: -17pt;text-align: justify;">Distribution Channels:</h3>
            <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
            <ol id="l5">
                <li data-list-text="4.1.">
                    <p style="padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: left;">Distribution Channel is defined
                        as [<span class="h2">Funcliq</span>];</p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="4.2.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: left;">Distribution
                        channel URL: <b>https://abrands2be.com/</b></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="4.3.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: left;"><a
                            href="mailto:<%=email%>"
                            style=" color: black; font-family:Calibri, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: none; font-size: 10pt;"
                            target="_blank">Email-Id of the Publisher: </a><a href="mailto:<%=email%>" target="_blank">
                            <%=email%>
                        </a></p>
                </li>
                <li data-list-text="4.4.">
                    <p style="padding-top: 4pt;padding-left: 49pt;text-indent: -20pt;text-align: left;">Contact Number
                        of the Publisher: <span class="h2">+91 <%=contact%></span></p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </li>
    </ol>
    <p style="text-indent: 0pt;text-align: left;"><br /></p>
